From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:57:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: Wake after a failed wake
 in suspend

When the controller sleeps idle and doesn't wake at a system suspend,
sn201202x_suspend() lets it sleep on and leaves the wake to resume. The
failed runtime resume left its error in power.runtime_error, though,
and while that is set rpm_resume() refuses with -EINVAL. So the resume
returned -EINVAL, the controller stayed asleep with runtime PM
suspended, and the port went unserved until a reboot.

Clear the error in resume before waking the controller through runtime
PM, which pm_runtime_set_suspended() may do while the error is set: the
controller is in fact still asleep. The wake is then tried again, and a
second failure is reported as before.

sn201202x_sleep_from_idle_failed_wakeup_test covers this case and
failed without the change.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
index 30d472c3d8..a021f9b37e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
@@ -849,6 +849,12 @@ VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT int __maybe_unused sn201202x_resume(struct device *dev)
 	}
 	/* One that slept on from idle sleep wakes through runtime PM */
 	if (pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev)) {
+		/*
+		 * A wake that failed in suspend left its error with runtime PM, which then
+		 * refuses every resume. The controller is still asleep: say so and try again.
+		 */
+		if (dev->power.runtime_error)
+			pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 		err = pm_runtime_resume(dev);
 		if (err > 0)
 			err = 0;
